+Identify the research question and main contributions before deciding what deserves depth. Follow each important claim to its mechanism and strongest evidence, including appendices, discussion, limitations, and negative results that change its interpretation. Reuse earlier reading and consult a directly cited reference when it is needed to explain a core mechanism. Label preliminary coverage and record any source gaps.
+
+Choose emphasis by contribution. For algorithms, trace the mathematical mechanism, architecture, training objective, and experimental comparisons. For benchmarks, trace provenance, construction, labels, quality gates, difficulty, and scoring. For agents, trace workflow, tools, state, memory, planning, recovery, and cost where applicable. For systems, trace interfaces, interactions, runtime behavior, and trade-offs.
 
